  "conclusion": "The whitened (covariance-corrected) MM direction does NOT align with LR better than plain MM. Small ridge (real whitening) DEGRADES alignment; large ridge converges back to plain MM. Cause: d_model (2304) > n_train for every dataset, so the within-class covariance is rank-deficient and Sigma^-1 is noise-dominated. M&T's LR = Sigma^-1 theta_mm equivalence assumes n >> d, which is violated here. Therefore the LR-MM tilt cannot be attributed to the covariance correction at this model's dimensionality with these dataset sizes."
